    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is headlined by **Jackson Merrill** (73.40) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.00), who represent our highest-ceiling plays against Roki Sasaki and Walker Buehler, respectively. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from an elite matchup profile, with a 14% boost from the opposing SP skill and a noteworthy 2% bump due to Sasaki\u2019s slow delivery, which positions **Jackson Merrill** perfectly for a stolen base opportunity. **Kyle Tucker** remains a locked-in core play, leveraging favorable platoon dynamics against Buehler to anchor the outfield production. Further down the order, **Nasim Nunez** (65.68) earns a surprise start; while his lineup position (#8) is a negative, his projection is heavily buoyed by an opportunistic 4% boost based on the opposing pitcher's slow delivery, which we are prioritizing today due to the extreme scarcity of speed in our current roster construct.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary drivers of our infield configuration, specifically with **Josh Jung** (63.87) and **Andy Pages** (64.69). **Josh Jung** sees his score swell thanks to a favorable 16% SP skill factor against Corbin, while **Andy Pages** is expected to produce efficiently in a #2 hole against Buehler. Conversely, the toughest decision involved **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.20), who was relegated to the bench despite a strong BvP historical edge (8%) against Eovaldi. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the high-efficiency platoon pairings of **Coby Mayo** and **Curtis Mead** in our 1B/2B slots; while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is a perennial starter, his negative 16% SP skill adjustment against Eovaldi made him the most logical candidate to sit in favor of maximizing daily category output.\n\nWe must monitor the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors, most notably **Drake Baldwin**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jacob Wilson**. While we have projected their spots based on historical us